-- N5 grammar, part two.
--
-- Same rules as 009: every word authored here, nothing imported, everything
-- 'in-review' until a human signs it off.
--
-- On citations: `quote` is left NULL wherever the supporting text has not been
-- transcribed from the source in hand. A locator points a reviewer at where to
-- check; an invented quotation attributed to a named scholar would be exactly
-- the failure this layer exists to prevent, and is worse than no citation.

ON CONFLICT (language_id, slug) DO NOTHING;
